            "output": "$\\mathbb{S}^d$",
            "localization": "d is the intrinsic dimension; the domain is not replaced by a cube or a solid ball."
          },
          "code": "admissible_model_class",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "$X=\\mathbb{S}^d\\subset\\mathbb{R}^{d+1}$, where $d$ is the intrinsic dimension of the sphere. The known kernel $k$ is the squared-exponential kernel, with fixed known amplitude and positive length scale.",
            "The unknown objective belongs to the kernel's reproducing kernel Hilbert space $\\mathcal{H}_k$ on $X$ and satisfies $\\|f\\|_{\\mathcal{H}_k}\\le B$ and $B>0$. Continuity and compactness ensure that a minimum is attained."
          ],
          "geometry_refs": [
            "SO_ZO_G06_rand_expected_dom_e20d873982",
